#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:1
msgid "Dense scenes and survivors-style games"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:3
msgid ""
"Pixel worlds provide optional simulation controls for games with many "
"enemies, projectiles and pickups. Existing `act()`, `detect()` and "
"`detect_all()` calls keep their default behavior. Spatial simulation "
"queries and actor pooling currently require a pixel `World`; pooling uses"
" its standard world connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:8
msgid "Collision groups and offscreen simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:10
msgid "Assign groups explicitly and select which groups a projectile can hit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:25
msgid ""
"`collision_targets` is directional: it restricts what the querying actor "
"detects. `None` allows every group and an empty set detects none. Sprite "
"`layer` still only controls drawing order. A group's typed spatial index "
"is built on its first query, then updated when actors move, change group,"
" deactivate or leave the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:30
msgid ""
"Ordinary actor collision queries remain camera-filtered unless "
"`collision_worldwide` is enabled. `actor.detect_collisions(Enemy)` "
"explicitly checks overlaps independently of the camera and uses the "
"actor's hitbox mode. Use rectangles or circles when pixel-perfect mask "
"collisions are unnecessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:35
msgid "Neighbors and nearest targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:37
msgid ""
"`world.query_rect(rect, Enemy)` finds overlapping hitboxes. "
"`world.query_radius(position, radius, Enemy)` finds actor **centers** in "
"a circle. `world.find_nearest(position, Enemy, radius=300)` finds a "
"center within that radius, or returns `None`. Omitting the radius "
"searches the entire world with expanding spatial queries. These APIs use "
"world pixel coordinates, include offscreen actors and accept "
"`collision_group=\"enemy\"` and `exclude=player`. The position may also "
"be an Actor, in which case its center is used. Equal-distance nearest "
"targets are resolved by `actor_id`. Query result lists otherwise have no "
"ordering contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:46
msgid ""
"Keep a target between updates while it remains active and in range, "
"rather than reacquiring it for every projectile and every frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:49
msgid "Pooling projectiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:78
msgid ""
"`acquire()` returns `None` when the configured capacity is exhausted. "
"Call `release()` instead of `remove()` to reuse an actor. The reset "
"callback runs before activation and must reset game state such as health,"
" damage, lifetime and hit history. Construction and `on_setup()` run once"
" per pooled actor. Position, sensor and costume managers are retained "
"across releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:84
msgid ""
"Inactive actors leave drawing groups, spatial indices, blocking and event"
" dispatch. `actor.active = False` pauses timers bound directly to that "
"actor; reactivation restores its subscriptions. Pool release instead "
"cancels such timers to prevent them from firing during the next lifetime."
" Timers or closures owned by other objects must be managed by the game. "
"`clear()` permanently removes all pool-owned actors. Do not transfer "
"pooled actors between worlds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:91
msgid "Movement, thinking and animation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:93
msgid ""
"`actor.move_towards_fast(target, distance)` moves without changing its "
"facing direction. It clamps the step at the target and respects "
"destination blocking. It has the same discrete destination-blocking "
"limitation as normal movement; fast projectiles may require a swept "
"collision test in the game."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:98
msgid ""
"`move_towards()` continues to update direction; its scalar movement and "
"the scalar `get_distance_to()` implementation avoid creating small NumPy "
"arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:101
msgid ""
"Use `on_think()` for expensive decisions and `act()` for continuous "
"movement:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:120
msgid ""
"Thinking runs before movement. `act_interval` and `think_interval` count "
"world logic ticks, so they combine with `world.tick_rate` without "
"starving actors. `offscreen_act_interval` sets a minimum interval for "
"both hooks outside the camera. Intervals are staggered by actor ID. "
"Slower movement updates reduce travel speed unless the game compensates "
"for elapsed ticks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:126
msgid ""
"`collision_interval` optionally reduces automatic collision-event checks,"
" in rendered frames; direct collision queries remain immediate. This also"
" reduces temporal collision precision. `animation_interval > 1` overrides"
" the costume's animation frame interval and staggers actors. The default "
"value `1` preserves the existing `costume.animation_speed` behavior. "
"Dirty costume changes still render immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:133
msgid "Sharing transform work and bounding memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:135
msgid ""
"Set `actor.costume.shared_transform_cache = True` for repeated "
"scale/rotation work across identical sprite frames. This is opt-in "
"because hashing source pixels can outweigh cheap transforms. Content keys"
" detect source pixel changes; returned surfaces remain independently "
"mutable. The process-wide cache defaults to **32 MiB** and evicts least "
"recently used results:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:148
msgid ""
"Per-appearance pipeline caches discard previous dirty revisions "
"immediately. Keep decorative enemies non-rotatable unless their artwork "
"needs rotation; the default is already `is_rotatable = False`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/survivors.md:152
msgid ""
"Run `invoke benchmarks.pyodide` to measure targeting, grouped collision "
"events, pooled projectiles and a rendered swarm. Timings depend on scene "
"density, browser and machine; use the same environment for comparisons."
msgstr ""
